#====================================================================
# Draft: Samba wafsamba standalone packages on OHOS - waf invocation
#        chain, mandatory runtime probes, python bindings policy
#        (tdb 1.4.15)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-11055-WAFSAMBA-STANDALONE-BUILD-POLICY
trigger_tool:           waf|configure|python|conan|make
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        The configuration failed|Could not build a python embedded interpreter|unable to find library -lintl|mandatory failure for this one|Checking for HAVE_SECURE_MKSTEMP

severity:               3
category:               build-system, waf, ohos, python, configure
match_keywords:         wafsamba, samba, tdb, talloc, tevent, ldb, waf, buildtools, PYTHONHASHSEED, WAF_MAKE, IN_LAUNCH_DIR, mkstemp, mandatory probe, robust mutex, pyembed, pyext, lintl, disable-python

title:                  Samba wafsamba standalone libraries on OHOS: PYTHON-driven in-tree waf configure/make, non-fatal handling of sandbox-unpassable mandatory runtime probes (/tmp read-only + HMDFS mode normalization), and --disable-python for C-only packages

root_cause:             Samba-family standalone libraries (tdb/talloc/ldb/tevent) use the bundled Samba waf instead of autotools/cmake. configure is driven by lib/replace probes; several execute=True probes can never pass in the OHOS sandbox: (a) HAVE_SECURE_MKSTEMP hardcodes /tmp (read-only on OHOS, E002) and asserts file mode 0600, but HMDFS normalizes modes to 0640 (chmod ineffective, E046), and upstream marks this probe mandatory=True so configure aborts; (b) the pyembed test links via python3-config --embed flags, and the OHOS python config emits -lintl although musl has no libintl, so that fatal probe fails. The configure/make wrapper scripts additionally require $PYTHON to point at a usable python3 and must run in the source root (IN_LAUNCH_DIR makes the build standalone).

affected_scope:         All Samba wafsamba ecosystem standalone packages (tdb/talloc/ldb/tevent and same-family projects) on OHOS: lib/replace execute=True mandatory probes, python binding detection and waf wrapper invocation. Verified instance: tdb 1.4.15 (bundled waf 2.1.6, python 3.14.7).

verification_cmd:       PYTHON=python3 ./configure --prefix=$PREFIX --disable-python && make -j2 && make test

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           ohos-wafsamba-standalone-build-policy
rec_description:        Drive the build with `PYTHON=python3 ./configure --prefix=<pkg> [--disable-python] && make -jN && make test` from the source root (in-tree standalone build; the wrappers set PYTHONHASHSEED/WAF_MAKE themselves). Convert sandbox-unpassable mandatory runtime probes to non-fatal (patch mandatory=True -> False) and accept the truthful "not found" result so lib/replace builds its bundled replacements; never relax the 0600 assertion or hardcode a device-only path. For C-only packages use the official --disable-python and add a wscript testonly guard so python binding tests are explicitly skipped rather than false-failing.
rec_command:            PYTHON=python3 ./configure --prefix=${PREFIX} --disable-python && make -j2 && make test
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/t/tdb/1.4.15/patches/0001-lib-replace-wscript.patch + 0002-wscript.patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      waf-cross-answers-file
fallback_description:   If a probe must yield a positive answer, evaluate waf --cross-answers with per-item justification that the answer matches real target semantics. tdb 1.4.15 did not need it: the bundled lib/replace implementations are exercised by the full upstream test suite, so the "not found" result stays truthful and functional.
fallback_command:       python3 buildtools/bin/waf --help   # lists --cross-compile/--cross-answers options
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       hardcode /dev/shm|point probe at device-only path|relax the 0600 assertion|chmod.*probe|inject -D__OHOS__
forbid_1_reason:        R8/PF5 forbid platform macros in patches; relaxing the secure-mkstemp assertion or redirecting the probe to a device-only path fakes a passing check instead of using lib/replace's bundled implementation; hardcoded device paths do not survive CI.
forbid_1_consequence:   Deceptive-adaptation finding in W4/preflight review; non-reproducible CI builds.

principles:             minimal-patch, platform-agnostic-fix, real-evidence-over-assumption
